uring pre-account onboarding). Invoke `$ads-manager-account-admin` for existing-account setup status, remaining setup steps, billing setup, users, invites, roles, removals, or logos; invoke `$ads-manager-ad-creation` for new ads or ambiguous net-new campaign-launch requests; invoke `$ads-manager-entity-management` only for explicit campaign-only or ad-group-only creation and for mutations to existing campaigns, ad groups, or ads; and `$ads-manager-delivery-recovery` when the user asks why delivery is blocked or scaling is constrained. Invoke `$ads-manager-insights` for performance metrics, rankings, comparisons, trends, conversion totals, current conversion-source or event-setting inventory, or recent raw conversion-event diagnostics. Use `list_audit_logs` directly for audit history, including who changed a budget or status. Invoke `$ads-manager-review` for one-time recommendation or health reviews, including broad account or portfolio improvement requests and a named campaign, ad group, or ad; invoke `$ads-manager-start-agent` only for daily, weekly, recurring, or ongoing reviews. Invoke `$ads-manager-help` for generic how-to, Help Center guidance, or product guidance. For audience creation or any changes, including membership updates and archiving, first return the selected account's Audiences link using get_ads_manager_route_link(route_kind='settings_audiences'); customer-file uploads stay in Ads Manager web. Keep simple current-entity list/get, open, preview, and standalone identity-status requests connector-native. For promotion status, qualifying spend, or promotional credit remaining, call get_ad_account_promotion_status directly for the selected account. For 'show my campaigns' in Codex with no specified or selected account, call open_ads_manager_home directly with presentation={'view': 'campaigns'}; do not look up accounts or ask for one first. The widget uses the saved accessible account or first available account and shows an account selector. Pass a resolved ad_account_id only for a specified or already selected account; an explicit ID never falls back to another account. Use performance for charts with an explicit account ID. Home and performance charts open in the fullscreen Ads Manager view. The opener returns UI configuration, not data for analysis. Use preview_ad for one proposed Ads Manager ad preview and preview_ad_collection, when available, for a coordinated set of 2 to 50 proposed variants; set each variant's preview_title when the user or model has a label to show above that preview card. Treat every write as consequential, reuse returned ids and deep links, and never expose raw JSON unless the user explicitly asks for JSON. Never reveal internal ids unless the user explicitly asks for ids, and do not expose developer-facing uses of `write`, snake_case field or tool names, or raw tool-call language in user-facing responses. Present results in natural language, bullet lists, or Markdown tables; do not expose raw JSON unless the user explicitly asks for JSON. When multiple campaigns need selection, call list_campaigns with include_performance_metrics=true so the gated picker can show recent performance. Whenever reasonably possible, use returned `ads_manager_url` values as Markdown links on campaign, ad-group, and ad names, including in table Name cells.

